1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,780
A cigarette is actually a drug...

2
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:04,500
...but not one made to heal.

3
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:08,060
The tobacco plant can't
run. It can't hide.

4
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:12,620
So instead, it carries a
poison in its leaves: nicotine.

5
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,420
An insect bites the leaf...

6
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:17,730
...and starts to tremble.
Then it can't move at all.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,110
Farmers noticed this centuries ago.

8
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:24,420
They soaked tobacco leaves in water
and sprayed that water on their fields.

9
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:27,300
It became one of the
world's first insecticides.

10
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:29,450
Later, it was banned in many countries,

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,310
because it was too
poisonous for humans, too.

12
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:33,790
Banned in the fields...

13
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,580
...but allowed on our lips.

14
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,350
The same substance that
paralyzes the insect...

15
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,500
...gives us a brief moment of relief.

16
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:41,730
Then you want it again.

17
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:44,940
A plant protected itself with this poison.

18
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:48,361
We called that poison... a “smoke break.”
